Summary: Hurray!
Keywords: I did it!

First, I play nethack on a pc (the local sys admin doesn't like 
to share these days).      :-(

It all started with Blinky the Samurai who forgot to purchase some 
candles thus headed back to the mines just after completing his 
quest.  Big deal, right?  Well, Blinky had no magic protection and
I didn't feel like level teleporting.  So, naturally Blinky manages
to find polymorph trap.  With his armor gone and burdened, he manages
to stumble on a pit fiend.  The pit fiend calls in some friends, and
presto!  The bones level from hell!

First victim:  An archeologist just on his first trip through the
mines.  Didn't stand a chance.
Next Victim:  A valkarie with mojo steps on a sleeping gas trap
and somehow manages to stay asleep while being crushed.
Next Victim:  An elf, busily firing missles gets himself caught
between two pit fiends.  Did count as a good try, though.
Next Victim:  another elf.  Never saw it coming.
Final Victim:  A caveman with Grayswandir (from an early wish).
Didn't have speed intrinsic yet and ac was >0, and was only
level 5.  Quick death.  Very quick.

BTW, what are the odds of this level returning so many times?

Finally!  Victory is mine!  I solved it with a barbarian!  First,
I immediately recognized the level.  Ghosts were everywhere, and a
pit fiend was coming for me.  I had no missle weapons so I threw
everthing I could find at it.  Rocks, swords, gems, you name it.
I then decided to finish him like a man.  I'm standing on 
the stairs hacking it when it reads a scroll (cursed create monster).
So, I run up the stairs leaving his pets behind.  He of course
followed me, but was weekened enough for me to dispatch without
too much trouble.  Scratch one, two pit fiends to go.  So, I went
back down the stairs to start on the critters.  Decided to id
some scrolls before hacking, and was lucky enough to get taming.
(I still have a pet yeti, BTW).  So, I go after the other two
fiends.  I'm wearing elven boots and an elven cloak, so I manage
to sneak over to the valkarie pile and kick free mojo un-noticed.
Rusty and cursed, but better than a mattock.  So, I start in on 
the other two.  The room was dark, but the deceased valkary had
a functioning lamp.  I spotted one and went to dispose of it.  On
my way over to it, I walked onto another polymorph trap, only I
turned into something useful this time, a mummak (sp).  The 
problem was I now had no decent armor.  When I returned to human,
I got in a few whacks but then had to #pray (AC was 10).  Odin was
well-pleased.  Once dispatched, I went back to the valks bones pile 
and put on all her cursed armor.  The third pit fiend went away 
without insident.  Artifacts on bones level: ToM, Mojo, Grayswandir.  
Also, cursed bag of holding and a cursed magic lamp (after mines 
turned into GDSM), and some cursed 20 food rations.  My next #pray 
(making holy water) was quite impressive.  Almost my entire inventory
glowed amber one by one.  Thanks, Odin!

I did it!  The level shall haunt me know more!
